# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseService

### DESCRIPTION

Own the selected Phase's entry, assigned semantic/Human completion and mechanical progression. The normal factory publishes startGoalPhase, advanceGoalPhase, submitGoalPhaseWorkResult and submitGoalPhaseOrderedDecision. Session context resolves pending work and native state; callers supply business inputs or requested results, not control envelopes or stages. Configured managed Step/Phase checks, review, closure and repository effects retain their owning authority. Other declarations are not additional normal public stages. Accepted review or a Human answer alone does not establish committed Step, Phase completion or release.

### OPERATION

#### advanceGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the actual ordered Phase associated with the invocation session. Normally no JSON argument is needed; supply only an instanceIdentity selector when the session has several targets, or sessionIdentity when the host has no session. Workflow resolves saved input and selects the next semantic work or mechanical checks/effects. The caller supplies no Step, transition, argv or receipt. Step closure is not whole-Phase completion. This declaration is not an execution grant; configured checks/effects retain their owning scope and authority.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseAdvanceResult

#### submitGoalPhaseWorkResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the assigned semantic value under result.value and its genuinely consumed result reference or execution evidence. Session context resolves the pending work; requestIdentity is needed only to distinguish applicable targets. Do not echo handle, run, revision, context snapshot or the issued envelope. The owning completion consumes actual result meaning and independent review evidence where required. No semantic result selects a cursor, command or closure permission.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkSubmissionResult

#### submitGoalPhaseOrderedDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the ordered GoalPhase answer under result.value with its actual evidence reference. Workflow resolves the pending Decision from session context, without a copied question, handle or context snapshot. Independent host Human evidence attests the selected question, participant and answer; authentication alone is not consent. ResumeAssignedWork requests assigned semantic work again without amending the Plan or refunding repair allowance. Defer and Cancel retain direction without issuing work or commands. Only owning advance selects following work.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionAnswer

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionSubmissionResult

#### startGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Start the selected Phase/repository with JSON input containing business Phase and repository references. Use actual invocation session context, or sessionIdentity when the host has none. Supply selectionIdentity only for genuinely ambiguous host selection; do not copy participant, execution controls or generated command fields. The host owns selection and actual authority. An entry acknowledgement is not Step review, document application, Git commit or Phase completion.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseStartResult

# SERVICE

## SplitPhaseService

### DESCRIPTION

Own SplitPhase entry, assigned semantic/Human completion, deterministic planning and document effects. Session context resolves native instance, planning context and pending work; callers return requested results without duplicated control fields. Workflow owns calibration, packing and progression to Preview or authorized managed Apply. Independent Human evidence and actual document scope remain with their owning host boundaries. Document-conflict handlers are unavailable, not a successful wait or terminal. A completion acknowledgement is not successful application.

### OPERATION

#### startSplitPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Start the selected source Phase with JSON input containing sourcePhaseIdentity, invocationMode and optional proposalReference. Actual session context and host selection resolve participant and allocation; use sessionIdentity or selectionIdentity only when needed. Do not send the generated Start command or copied control fields. A successful entry returns the owning Start observation, not completed partitioning or changed documents. The host owns source authority and managed execution scope.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseStartResult

#### submitPartitionSemanticResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Return partition judgment under result.value for the session's pending task. Enriched supplies only requested unknown estimates, semantic boundary judgments and their actual evidence; DecisionNeeded is semantic data, not Human consent. Workflow resolves the assigned destination internally, without result-reference, context or envelope echoes. Workflow owns calibration, enumeration, packing and ranking. Completion acknowledges this task, not downstream document application; the caller does not select an admission stage or command.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult

#### advanceSplitPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the native instance and partition context resolved from the invocation session. Normally no JSON argument is needed; supply only necessary sessionIdentity, instanceIdentity or contextIdentity selectors. There is no caller-selected stage, candidate or command. Workflow absorbs mechanical work and returns the next semantic task, wait or terminal. The saved Start mode determines Preview or authorized managed Apply. Genuine scope/reasoning Decisions consume independently attested ProvideResolution or record Defer/Cancel. ALL-Built must not be converted into a Human task. Document-conflict semantic/Human handlers remain unavailable; unavailable capability is not a successful WAIT or Terminal. This declaration is not an execution grant.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceResult

#### submitHandoffScopeResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the handoff judgment under result.value for the session's pending task. Enriched supplies ordered producing/receiving subsets for the issued gaps; DecisionNeeded supplies no partial scopes. Supply actual semantic evidence once. Workflow resolves checkpoint and assigned destination internally, without control or reference echoes. Completion acknowledges this semantic boundary; it does not select downstream operations, transfer authority or apply documents.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSubmissionResult

#### submitReasoningResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Return only requested unknown-item classifications, rationale and actual evidence under result.value, or DecisionNeeded without partial assignments. Workflow resolves the session's pending reasoning task and its assigned result destination internally; no result-reference, checkpoint, context or envelope echo is needed. Workflow owns resulting data and objective-only continuation over the original frontier. A completion acknowledgement is not Preview, Apply or permission to select a stage or command.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSubmissionResult

#### submitSplitHumanDirection

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the pending Human answer under result.value with its actual result/evidence reference. Workflow resolves the Decision from session context; do not copy the whole question or control envelope. Independent host Human evidence attests the selected question and answer; an authenticated relay alone is not consent. ProvideResolution names separate interpretation data, while Defer and Cancel carry no resolution. Owning advance continues scope/reasoning or observes the stopped outcome. An answer acknowledgement is not document application. Document-conflict semantic/Human resolution is not installed. Duplicate-answer, replay and intermediate-recovery guarantees are outside this interface.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionAnswer

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionSubmissionResult

# SERVICE

## RepositoryHumanService

### DESCRIPTION

Independent Human channel for a retained RepositorySync semantic conflict that
could not be decided. Present the original base/local/remote text and rationale;
do not infer consent from AI output or login identity. Only the exact issued
Decision completion may return the Human answer. This declaration installs no
channel, command executor or source/remote permission.

### OPERATION

#### presentRepositoryConflictDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Present only the exact Workflow-issued conflict question, including its original
texts and rationale, through the independent Human channel. Return the declared
answer through the assigned completion route; do not substitute an AI judgment
or infer consent from login identity. Workflow verifies the answer and owns later
resolution effects. This operation performs no file, Git or synchronization effect.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictAnswer

# SERVICE

## RepositorySyncService

### DESCRIPTION

Own repository convergence through five normal Operations: Start, advance and assigned conflict/review/Human completion. Session context resolves selected native state and pending work. Workflow owns fetch, preservation, integration, validation, commit, push and final observation through configured fixed managed Git/check capabilities, delegating only requested semantic results or Human answers. Other declarations are not additional normal public stages. Host scope, effect authority and independent evidence remain with their consuming boundaries. A WAIT or accepted review without the actual final repository outcome is not convergence.

### OPERATION

#### startRepositorySync

##### DESCRIPTION

Start RepositorySync with JSON input containing repositoryIdentity, localBranch, trackingRemote, trackingBranch, remoteEndpointIdentity and syncMode. Invocation session context and host selection resolve participant and allocation; use sessionIdentity or selectionIdentity only when needed, not generated command/control copies. The entry response is not a fetch, push or synchronized repository. Start grants no command or remote authority. Owning advance performs managed effects within actual configured selection and permissions.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncStartInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncStartResult

#### advanceRepositorySync

##### DESCRIPTION

Advance the RepositorySync instance associated with the invocation session. Normally no JSON argument is needed; supply only a necessary instanceIdentity selector or sessionIdentity when the host has no session. Workflow absorbs fixed managed Git/check progression and returns the next conflict/review/Human work, wait or final convergence. The caller supplies no stage, repository path, argv or receipt. Actual configured scope, effect authority and independent evidence stay with their owning boundaries. A fetched WAIT or accepted review is not final convergence; this interface promises no intermediate recovery or replay guarantee.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncAdvanceInput

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncAdvanceResult

#### submitRepositorySyncWorkResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the assigned conflict judgment under result.value with its genuinely consumed result reference/evidence. Session context resolves the pending WorkOrder; no handle, run, revision, context or issued-envelope echo is required. The owning completion consumes conflict coverage and meaning. A resolution proposal grants no command, file-write, commit or push authority and is not convergence.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictSubmissionResult

#### submitNativeMergeReview

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the assigned merge-review judgment under result.value and its actual result/evidence reference. Workflow resolves pending work from session context; independent host evidence attests the selected review and actual reviewer. No copied WorkOrder or control envelope is required. Review acceptance alone grants no repair, command, commit, push or convergence authority.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncNativeMergeReviewResult

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncNativeMergeReviewSubmissionResult

#### submitRepositoryConflictDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Return the pending conflict Decision answer under result.value and its actual result/evidence reference. Session context resolves the selected question without a complete question or control-envelope echo. Independent host Human evidence attests that selected question and answer; authentication alone is not consent. ProvideResolution supplies actual conflict text within the bounded policy; Defer and Cancel carry no file proposal. Owning advance chooses materialization, validation, review and authorized convergence. The answer grants no file, command or remote authority. An unavailable Human handler is not successful completion.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictAnswer

##### PARAMETER

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------+------|--------------|
| arg1 | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictSubmissionResult

# SERVICE

## RepositoryConflictService

### DESCRIPTION

Required semantic SPI for only Workflow-issued native text conflicts. Return a
bounded resolution proposal or DecisionNeeded through its assigned completion
operation. Do not choose a stage, modify files, execute commands, grant Human
consent or assert validation, commit, push or synchronization acceptance.

### OPERATION

#### resolveRepositoryMergeConflicts

##### DESCRIPTION

Evaluate only the issued native text conflicts and return a bounded resolution
proposal or DecisionNeeded in RepositorySyncConflictResult. Do not modify files,
execute external commands, choose a transition or assert Human consent. Workflow
owns materialization, validation, independent review and convergence; the proposal
alone neither resolves the repository nor grants command authority.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncConflictResult

# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseImplementationService

### DESCRIPTION

Required semantic implementation SPI for the selected ordered Phase. Return only
the result of the assigned Step implementation, not a review or repair result.
External commands, native evidence admission and all transitions belong to the
owning Workflow. This declaration alone installs no semantic worker or executor.

### OPERATION

#### implementGoalPhaseStep

##### DESCRIPTION

Perform the implementation selected by GoalPhaseWorkRequest's original plan,
Step and purpose, and return completion or an explicit decision-needed result.
Return only the assigned semantic result; do not select another Step, execute
external commands, supply native receipts or claim review, commit or Phase
closure. Workflow observes the actual candidate and owns mechanical validation
and subsequent independent review.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseOrderedHumanService

### DESCRIPTION

Required Human channel for a Workflow-issued ordered GoalPhase semantic decision.
Return only an exact declared answer through its assigned completion Operation.
The question retains the original work and requesting semantic result; neither
presentation nor an answer selects commands, another Plan or new repair authority.

### OPERATION

#### presentOrderedGoalDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Present the original assigned work, retained requesting result and Workflow
choices to the Human. Return ResumeAssignedWork, Defer or Cancel with rationale
as GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionAnswer. Do not forge consent, choose a successor
stage, approve a review, edit files or execute commands. Independent Human
evidence admission remains the owning host's responsibility.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseOrderedDecisionAnswer

# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseRepairWorkService

### DESCRIPTION

Required semantic repair SPI for the owning ordered Phase's issued repair work.
Respect the original selected plan and explicit repair directive; do not create
another repair allowance or reset accounting. Workflow owns repair selection,
mechanical checks and independent review. Declaration alone grants no command,
review or closure authority and installs no repair worker.

### OPERATION

#### repairGoalPhaseStep

##### DESCRIPTION

Repair only the assigned Step under its issued repair directive and retained
review context. Return completion or an explicit decision-needed result through
the assigned completion route. Do not expand the repair scope, reset counters,
execute external commands or substitute a passing review. Workflow observes the
changed candidate and selects the required checks and independent follow-up.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseStepReviewService

### DESCRIPTION

Required independent, read-only semantic review SPI for the actual selected Step
candidate and its retained validation context. Workflow supplies the complete
issued review subject and owns result admission, repair selection and mechanical
closure. Review is neither command authority nor a Step commit; this declaration
alone installs no reviewer or independent evidence verifier.

### OPERATION

#### reviewGoalPhaseStep

##### DESCRIPTION

Independently review the complete assigned Step candidate and selected check
evidence in GoalPhaseWorkRequest. Return only the semantic decision, summary and
findings through the assigned completion route. Do not repair the candidate or
execute external commands. Workflow verifies independent review evidence and
owns repair or closure; a passing subset is not complete candidate acceptance.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

# SERVICE

## GoalPhaseReviewService

### DESCRIPTION

Required independent, read-only semantic review SPI for the whole original
selected Phase, including every retained closed Step and required final checks.
Do not narrow acceptance to the latest Step or a passing subset. Workflow owns
review admission and repository closure; declaration alone installs no reviewer,
independent evidence verifier or commit/push executor.

### OPERATION

#### reviewGoalPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Independently review the whole selected Phase and its actual issued candidate,
completed Step history and final check evidence. Return only the semantic review
result through the assigned completion route. Do not repair, execute external
commands or assert Phase completion from partial success. Workflow verifies the
independent evidence and owns any required repair or authorized repository closure.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

GoalPhaseWorkResult

# SERVICE

## MergeReviewService

### DESCRIPTION

Required independent semantic review SPI for a validated original pending merge.
The reviewer evaluates the complete issued candidate and selected evidence,
including parents, tree and required checks, without performing Git effects.
Workflow admits the result and owns deterministic commit/push/convergence or
required repair/Human follow-up. Review acceptance is not command authority or
successful repository synchronization, and unresolved evidence must stay explicit.

### OPERATION

#### reviewNativePendingMerge

##### DESCRIPTION

Independently review the actual full pending merge against both parents and
selected validation results. Return only decision, rationale and path-scoped
findings through the assigned completion. Do not repair or invoke commands.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncNativeMergeReviewRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncNativeMergeReviewResult

